+---
+title: Testing click.utils to full line+branch coverage
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 54474 }
+touches:
+  - tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- Platform-specific branches of get_app_dir are reached by monkeypatching `click.utils.WIN` (imported name, patch on click.utils, not _compat) and `sys.platform`, plus setenv/delenv for APPDATA, LOCALAPPDATA, XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
+- `_expand_args` imports `glob` inside the function, so `monkeypatch.setattr(glob, "glob", ...)` raising `re.error` is how to hit the invalid-pattern fallback; current Python's glob does not raise re.error on its own.
+- `_detect_program_name()` defaults are tested by `monkeypatch.setitem(sys.modules, "__main__", fake_module)` and patching `sys.argv`; under `python -m pytest` the real __main__ is pytest's.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Asserting a fake stream only receives the echoed bytes: `_compat._is_binary_writer` probes the stream with `write(b"")` then `write("")`, so a text-only fake also records an empty string write.
+
+## Watch out
+- pyproject sets `filterwarnings = ["error"]`: touching deprecated `click.utils.<name>` aliases (LazyFile, safecall, get_text_stream, ...) fails unless wrapped in `pytest.warns(DeprecationWarning)`.
+- `echo(b"...", file=io.StringIO())` raises TypeError (no binary writer found, falls through to text write); that is the existing behaviour, not a test bug.
+- The "unclosed database" ResourceWarning lines at the end of the suite are pre-existing and unrelated to utils tests.
